# CHAPTER 8 · IDE MOVES ON YOUR SETUP

Everything VSCode gave you exists in this config — faster, and it
composes with chapters 1-7. This chapter is pure workflow: no text
exercises, instead run things in a real code file. Open one of your
Python or VHDL files in another window and work through it.

## 8.1 FINDING THINGS: TELESCOPE

- `<leader>ff`{normal} find files · `<leader>fa`{normal} include
  hidden/ignored
- `<leader>fw`{normal} live grep the whole project (your Ctrl+Shift+F)
- `<leader>fb`{normal} open buffers · `<leader>fo`{normal} recent files
- `<leader>fz`{normal} fuzzy find IN the current buffer
- `<leader>fh`{normal} search all of vim's help — use this constantly
  while doing this course

Inside any Telescope picker: `<C-q>`{normal} dumps ALL matches into
the quickfix list. grep "fifo_full" → `<C-q>`{normal} →
`:cnext`{vim} through every hit in the project. That one key turns
search results into a work queue.

Try them now — run this line with `>>`{normal}:

    :Telescope keymaps

That picker fuzzy-searches EVERY mapping in your setup. Forgot a key
from this course? It is in there.

## 8.2 CODE INTELLIGENCE: LSP

Your servers (pyright, clangd, lua_ls...) attach automatically.

- `gd`{normal} go to definition · `gD`{normal} declaration ·
  `<leader>D`{normal} type definition
- `K`{normal} hover docs (press again to enter the float, `q`{normal}
  to leave)
- `grr`{normal} references · `gri`{normal} implementation ·
  `gra`{normal} code action — built into nvim 0.11+
- `<leader>ra`{normal} rename symbol project-wide (NvChad renamer)
- `]d`{normal} / `[d`{normal} next/previous diagnostic ·
  `<leader>ds`{normal} all diagnostics in a list
- `<leader>fm`{normal} format file (conform, with LSP fallback)

THE LOOP that replaces ctrl-clicking around VSCode: `gd`{normal} to
dive in, `<C-o>`{normal} to surface, `K`{normal} instead of opening
the file at all. Combine with chapter 6: definition three files deep,
`<C-o>`{normal} `<C-o>`{normal} `<C-o>`{normal} home.

Completion is nvim-cmp: `<Tab>`{normal}/`<S-Tab>`{normal} walk
items, `<CR>`{normal} accepts.

## 8.3 GIT WITHOUT LEAVING

Your gitsigns + diffview keys:

- `<leader>gh`{normal} preview hunk under cursor ·
  `<leader>gs`{normal} stage it · `<leader>gr`{normal} reset it
- `<leader>gb`{normal} blame line · `<leader>gB`{normal} toggle
  inline blame
- `<leader>gv`{normal} full diff view · `<leader>gV`{normal} history
  of the current file
- `<leader>cm`{normal} / `<leader>gt`{normal} Telescope commits /
  status

Hunk-level staging from inside the buffer beats the VSCode source
control panel: review with `<leader>gh`{normal}, stage with
`<leader>gs`{normal}, move on. No context switch.

## 8.4 TERMINALS, TREE, BUFFERS — YOUR KEYS

- `<A-i>`{normal} floating terminal · `<A-h>`{normal} /
  `<A-v>`{normal} split terminals (toggle on/off)
- `<Esc><Esc>`{normal} leave terminal mode · `<leader>tq`{normal}
  close a terminal buffer
- `<leader>e`{normal} file tree · `<Tab>`{normal} /
  `<S-Tab>`{normal} buffers · `<leader>x`{normal} close buffer
- `<leader>fs`{normal} save · `<leader>qq`{normal} quit everything ·
  `<C-c>`{normal} copy file/selection to system clipboard
- `jk`{normal} leaves insert mode — your fingers never visit Esc
- `<leader>/`{normal} toggle comment (or pure vim: `gcc`{normal} for
  a line, `gc`{normal} + motion — gcip comments a paragraph)
- `<leader>ch`{normal} the NvChad cheatsheet of every mapping ·
  `<leader>wK`{normal} which-key with everything

## 8.5 GRADUATION PROJECT

Do one real task end to end without the file tree and without the
mouse:

1. `<leader>fw`{normal} to find the code, `<C-q>`{normal} it into
   quickfix.
2. Fix the first site, `cgn`{normal}-style or with `.`{normal}, then
   `:cnext`{vim} through the rest.
3. `gd`{normal} / `<C-o>`{normal} to verify a caller, `K`{normal}
   instead of opening docs.
4. Review your work hunk by hunk with `<leader>gh`{normal}, stage
   with `<leader>gs`{normal}.
5. `<A-i>`{normal}, run the tests, `<Esc><Esc>`{normal},
   `<leader>qq`{normal}. Done.

When that loop feels boring, you have left VSCode for good.

Key reading: [lsp](lsp), [telescope.nvim](telescope.nvim),
[gitsigns-usage](gitsigns-usage), [terminal](terminal)

